# Shell scripts keep LF endings on every platform they are checked out on.
#
# Not a style preference. A carriage return at the end of the shebang line
# becomes part of the interpreter path, and the kernel then looks for a program
# named "bash\r" and does not find one. A checkout with autocrlf enabled would
# produce exactly that, so the attribute is pinned here rather than left to
# whatever each contributor has configured.
*.sh text eol=lf
